# Tells every mounted SSD which blocks are free. The installer mounts ext4 and
# xfs without `discard`, so without this a freed block is never reported and
# the drive's write speed and wear degrade as it fills with blocks it believes
# are still in use. btrfs and f2fs already discard as they free blocks, so on
# them this is a cheap second pass. A filesystem whose device cannot discard
# is skipped by fstrim itself.
#
# Daily, and at midday rather than overnight: fstrim cannot touch a timefile,
# so there is no `-t` and a slot the machine was OFF for is simply missed. A
# desktop switched off every night would never reach a 03:00 slot. ext4 skips
# a block group it has trimmed and freed nothing in since, so on a mounted ext4
# the runs after the first cost little.
#
# -s 20h: a machine ASLEEP at the slot runs it once when it wakes, within the
# day.
fstrim  -H 12 -M 47 -s 20h  --  fstrim -a
